   "speakerNote": "Now a real-scale version of our problem: bring 100 people from 15 countries to this conference by the 23rd, for under 30,000 euros. By hand, that is weeks of an organiser's work. A lead splits the job into three groups. Transport has two teams: flights for the long distances, trains and buses for the short ones. Accommodation has hotels, and catering for the lunches. Correspondence has one worker per attendee, who speaks for that person. Each team's work is checked. And the teams don't call each other: they write into one living plan and read what the others wrote. Flights notes that twelve people land after ten at night; Hotels reads it and holds late check-ins; attendee 37 needs a step-free room. The plan is how they talk.",
